---
// The hook + the single most persuasive object on the page: a rendered product
// surface refusing to guess. No competitor's landing page can show this.
---

<section id="top" class="relative overflow-hidden pt-16 pb-20 md:pt-24 md:pb-28">
  <div class="shell grid items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow rise">Honest &middot; self-hosted &middot; grounded in research</p>

      <h1 class="rise mt-6 text-[clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4.25rem)]">
        The health companion that<br class="hidden sm:block" />
        <span class="italic text-accent-soft">refuses to flatter you.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="rise mt-7 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Healthee reads your wearable, then tells you the truth: every interpretation cited to
        graded research, every number carrying its own confidence, and
        <span class="text-ink">&ldquo;not enough data&rdquo;</span> whenever that is the honest
        answer. No green rings. No grading on a curve.
      </p>

      <div class="rise mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a href="#self-host" class="btn btn-primary">Self-host it today</a>
        <a href="#honesty" class="btn btn-ghost">Watch it refuse &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p class="rise mt-6 max-w-md text-sm text-ink-faint">
        You own the hardware and the data. You pay only for the intelligence &mdash; and only if
        you want it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The refusal card -->
    <div class="rise lg:justify-self-end">
      <figure class="surface w-full max-w-md p-6 sm:p-7" aria-label="Example: the product declining to score with insufficient data">
        <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
          <span class="eyebrow">Recovery &middot; today</span>
          <span class="chip chip-warn chip-dot">not enough data</span>
        </figcaption>

        <hr class="hairline my-5" />

        <p class="font-serif text-2xl leading-snug">
          I&rsquo;m not going to give you a recovery score today.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Only <span class="mono text-ink">2</span> of the last
          <span class="mono text-ink">7</span> nights have usable overnight HRV. A recovery number
          needs a stable baseline; inventing one would be worse than staying quiet.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <span class="chip">coverage&nbsp;·&nbsp;29%</span>
          <span class="chip">baseline&nbsp;·&nbsp;insufficient</span>
          <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">fix&nbsp;·&nbsp;5+ nights worn</span>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <p class="mt-3 pl-1 text-xs text-ink-faint mono">
        A rendered example of the honesty contract, not a live reading.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- honest status ribbon -->
  <div class="shell mt-16 md:mt-20">
    <div
      class="rise flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 border-y border-line py-4 text-sm text-ink-soft"
    >
      <span class="eyebrow">Where it stands</span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">live</span> Backend: deployed &amp; multi-tenant
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="chip chip-dot">building</span> Mobile app: in progress (Phase 2)
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="chip chip-dot">closed</span> Public sign-ups: not open yet
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
